aracter-based `chunk_size=500` means 500 characters.\n","- Token-based `chunk_size=500` means 500 tokens when the splitter is configured with a tokenizer.\n","\n","The parameter name is the same, but the unit is different.\n","\n","## Chunking Strategy Comparison\n","\n","Here is a comparison of the major techniques.\n","\n","| Strategy        | Main principle                                | Complexity  | Best use case                   |\n","| --------------- | --------------------------------------------- | ----------- | ------------------------------- |\n","| Fixed-size      | Split by characters or tokens                 | Low         | Basic prototypes                |\n","| Sentence-based  | Split by sentence boundaries                  | Low         | General prose                   |\n","| Recursive       | Split using hierarchical separators           | Low–Medium  | General-purpose RAG             |\n","| Token-based     | Respect tokenizer limits                      | Low–Medium  | LLM input constraints           |\n","| Semantic        | Split based on meaning changes                | High        | Topic-rich documents            |\n","| Structure-aware | Preserve document structure                   | Medium–High | PDFs, docs, websites            |\n","| Parent-child    | Retrieve small chunks, supply larger context  | High        | Complex RAG                     |\n","| Late chunking   | Contextualize before pooling chunk embeddings | High        | Long-context semantic retrieval |\n","\n","My recommendation for a typical technical-document RAG system:\n","\n","1. Start with structure-aware recursive chunking.\n","2. Use token-based size limits.\n","3. Add moderate overlap.\n","4. Add reranking.\n","5. Evaluate semantic chunking or parent-child retrieval if needed.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":11,"id":"d58d6b91","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-23T06:09:29.424547Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-23T06:09:29.424159Z