,"papermill":{"duration":0.019185,"end_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.252342+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.233157+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["# for metric, score in results.items():\n","#     print(f\"{metric}: {score:.4f}\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":44,"id":"91c5d002","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.27604Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.275651Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.280568Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.279522Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.019456,"end_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.282801+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.263345+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["# from ranx import Run, compare\n","\n","# bm25_run = Run(bm25_results, name=\"BM25\")\n","# dense_run = Run(dense_results, name=\"Dense\")\n","# hybrid_run = Run(hybrid_results, name=\"Hybrid\")\n","\n","# report = compare(\n","#     qrels=qrels,\n","#     runs=[bm25_run, dense_run, hybrid_run],\n","#     metrics=[\n","#         \"precision@5\",\n","#         \"recall@5\",\n","#         \"mrr@5\",\n","#         \"ndcg@5\"\n","#     ]\n","# )"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":45,"id":"3cb99d60","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.308784Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.308356Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.313185Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.312144Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.021523,"end_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.315401+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.293878+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["# report"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"13e9cd5c","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.011152,"end_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.337675+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.326523+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Generation metrics\n","\n","| Metric                      | What it measures                                                  |\n","| --------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n","| Answer correctness          | Whether the answer matches the ground truth                       |\n","| Faithfulness / groundedness | Whether claims are supported by retrieved evidence                |\n","| Answer relevance            | Whether the response addresses the question                       |\n","| Citation precision          | Whether cited passages support the claims                         |\n","| Citation coverage           | Whether claims that require evidence are cited                    |\n","| Abstention quality          | Whether the system declines to answer when evidence is inadequate |\n","\n","Frameworks such as RAGAS and LangSmith can help automate parts of this evaluation. MongoDB's RAG evaluation tutorial also demonstrates evaluating embeddings, retrieval, generation, and the overall application separately.\n","\n","LLM-as-a-judge metrics are useful, but they are not ground truth. Validate them against human-reviewed examples, especially for high-impact applications.\n","\n","## An evaluation loop\n","\n","Use this sequence when improving a RAG application:\n","\n","```\n","Create a fixed evaluation dataset\n","    |\n","Measure baseline retrieval and answer quality\n","    |\n","Change one component: chunks, embeddings, top-K, or reranker\n","    |\n","Re-run the same evaluation set\n","    |\n","Keep changes that improve quality without unacceptable cost or latency\n","```\n","\n","Don't change five things simultaneously. If you do, you may not know which change caused the improvement or regression. "]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"6083f479","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.010888,"end_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.359549+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.348661+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Good RAG evaluation score\n","\n","There is no universal benchmark that guarantees a production-ready RAG application. However, you can establish initial engineering targets.\n","\n","| Metric | Example target |\n","| --- | --- |\n","| Retrieval Precision@5 | ≥ 0.80 |\n","| Retrieval Recall@5 | ≥ 0.85 |\n","| Faithfulness | ≥ 0.90 |\n","| Answer Relevancy | ≥ 0.85 |\n","| Context Precision | ≥ 0.80 |\n","| Context Recall | ≥ 0.85 |\n","| Answer Correctness | ≥ 0.85 |\n","\n","These are suggested starting targets, not industry standards. Evaluate against your own domain, risk level, and ground-truth dataset.\n","\n","### Understanding the Results\n","\n","The results above clearly demonstrate the **precision-recall tradeoff** in retrieval systems as we vary K from 5 to 20 to 50:\n","\n","**Precision@K Trends (generally decreases as K increases):**\n","\n","- **At K=5**: Most queries achieve very high precision (0.80-1.00), with 8 out of 10 queries having perfect precision (1.00). This means nearly all retrieved documents are highly relevant.\n","  \n","- **At K=20**: Precision starts to decline for some queries:\n","  - \"electronics in computing devices\" drops to 0.80 (from 1.00)\n","  - \"Windows operating system\" drops to 0.65 (from 0.80)\n","  - \"motorcycles maintenance\" drops to 0.95 (from 1.00)\n","  \n","- **At K=50**: Precision decreases further as we retrieve more documents:\n","  - \"computer graphics\" drops to 0.88 (from 1.00)\n","  - \"electronics in computing devices\" drops to 0.66 (from 0.80)\n","  - \"Windows operating system\" drops to 0.60 (from 0.65)\n","  - \"historical influence of politics\" remains around 0.50-0.52 (the lowest across all K values)\n","\n","**Recall@K Trends (increases as K increases):**\n","\n","- **At K=5**: Recall is very low (~0.01 or 1%), meaning only about 1% of all relevant documents are retrieved\n","  \n","- **At K=20**: Recall triples to ~0.03 (3%), capturing more relevant documents\n","  \n","- **At K=50**: Recall increases to 0.05-0.08 (5-8%), capturing approximately 8 times more relevant documents than K=5\n","\n","**Key Observations:**\n","\n","1. **The tradeoff is clear**: As K increases, we retrieve more of the total relevant documents (higher recall), but at the cost of including some irrelevant documents (lower precision).\n","\n","2. **Some queries are harder than others**: The query \"historical influence of politics on society\" consistently shows the lowest precision (0.40-0.52), suggesting that this query is semantically ambiguous or the category \"talk.politics.misc\" is harder to distinguish from related categories.\n","\n","3. **For RAG systems, K=5 to K=20 is often optimal**: These values provide high precision (most retrieved documents are relevant) while keeping the context size manageable for the LLM. Even though recall is low, the goal is to find the *most relevant* documents, not *all* relevant documents.\n","\n","4. **Recall remains relatively low even at K=50**: This is expected since each category contains hundreds of documents (500-600), so retrieving 50 documents only captures ~8-10% of the total relevant documents. To achieve high recall, we would need K values in the hundreds, which would severely impact precision and be impractical for RAG applications.\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"474a22d8","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.010709,"end_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.381433+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.370724+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# RAGAS\n","\n","**RAGAS (Retrieval Augmented Generation Assessment)** is an open-source framework designed to evaluate the performance and quality of Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems.\n","\n","It helps developers measure how well an AI system:\n","\n","- Retrieves relevant information from a knowledge base.\n","- Generates accurate answers based on retrieved information.\n","- Avoids hallucinations.\n","- Provides answers that are relevant to the user's question.\n","- Uses retrieved context effectively.\n","\n","<div style=\"display: flex; gap: 10px;\">\n","  <img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/masum184e/handbook/main/static/img/ai-engineering/ragas_framwork_1.png\" width=\"33%\">\n","  <img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/masum184e/handbook/main/static/img/ai-engineering/ragas_framwork_2.png\" width=\"33%\">\n","  <img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/masum184e/handbook/main/static/img/ai-engineering/ragas_framwork_3.png\" width=\"33%\">\n","</div>\n","\n","RAGAS is especially useful when building AI applications such as:\n","\n","- Chatbots using company documents.\n","- AI-powered question-answering systems.\n","- PDF-based chatbots.\n","- Enterprise knowledge assistants.\n","- Customer support AI.\n","- LLM applications using vector databases.\n","\n","The key idea is that a RAG system cannot be evaluated only by checking the final answer. We must also evaluate the retrieval process and the relationship between the retrieved context and the generated answer.\n","\n","**Why need RAGAS for RAG?**\n","\n","Now, how do we know the answer is good?\n","\n","We need to check:\n","\n","- Was the correct document retrieved?\n","- Is the answer factually correct?\n","- Is the answer supported by the retrieved document?\n","- Does the answer address the question?\n","\n","This is where RAGAS comes into play.\n","\n","## RAGAS architecture\n","\n","A typical RAGAS evaluation pipeline works as follows:\n","\n","![RAGAS Pipeline](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/masum184e/handbook/main/static/img/ai-engineering/ragas_pipeline.png)\n","\n","RAGAS takes evaluation data and uses various metrics to calculate scores.\n","\n","The evaluation dataset generally contains:\n","\n","| Field          | Description                           |\n","| -------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n","| `question`     | The user query                        |\n","| `contexts`     | Documents retrieved by the RAG system |\n","| `answer`       | Generated response                    |\n","| `ground_truth` | Reference answer, if available        |\n","\n","Depending on the metric, RAGAS may use the question, contexts, answer, ground truth, an LLM, or an embedding model.\n","\n","## Evaluation Dataset\n","\n","One of the most important aspects of RAGAS is the evaluation dataset. A dataset provides sample questions and the information required to evaluate the RAG system."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":46,"id":"f9c34f5a","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.4051Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.40474Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.434013Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.433022Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.043983,"end_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.436258+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.392275+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["\n","from datasets import Dataset\n","\n","data = {\n","    \"question\": [\n","        \"What is the refund period?\",\n","        \"What is the capital of Bangladesh?\"\n","    ],\n","\n","    \"contexts\": [\n","        [\"Customers can request refunds within 30 days.\"],\n","        [\"Dhaka is the capital of Bangladesh.\"]\n","    ],\n","\n","    \"answer\": [\n","        \"Customers can request a refund within 30 days.\",\n","        \"The capital of Bangladesh is Dhaka.\"\n","    ],\n","\n","    \"ground_truth\": [\n","        \"The refund period is 30 days.\",\n","        \"Dhaka is the capital of Bangladesh.\"\n","    ]\n","}\n","\n","dataset = Dataset.from_dict(data)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":47,"id":"404b86c3","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.46216Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.461294Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.466399Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.465522Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.020322,"end_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.468529+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.448207+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Dataset({\n","    features: ['question', 'contexts', 'answer', 'ground_truth'],\n","    num_rows: 2\n","})\n"]}],"source":["print(dataset)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":48,"id":"ad2032f3","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.492284Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.491875Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.499752Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.498694Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.022243,"end_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.501723+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.47948+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["{'question': 'What is the refund period?', 'contexts': ['Customers can request refunds within 30 days.'], 'answer': 'Customers can request a refund within 30 days.', 'ground_truth': 'The refund period is 30 days.'}\n"]}],"source":["print(dataset[0])"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"bd363fa7","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.011247,"end_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.524022+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.512775+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Dataset fields explained\n","\n","| Field          | Meaning                                   |\n","| -------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n","| `question`     | The query submitted by the user           |\n","| `contexts`     | Context retrieved from the knowledge base |\n","| `answer`       | The RAG system's generated response       |\n","| `ground_truth` | The expected/reference answer             |\n","\n","In newer RAGAS APIs, you may see names such as `user_input`, `retrieved_contexts`, `response`, and `reference`. These names depend on the dataset and metric interface being used.\n","\n","### Importance of ground truth\n","\n","Ground truth allows RAGAS to evaluate:\n","\n","- Whether the retrieval system found the necessary information.\n","- Whether the answer matches the expected facts.\n","- Whether important information was omitted.\n","\n","However, not every metric requires ground truth.\n","\n","| Metric              | Ground truth required? |\n","| ------------------- | ---------------------- |\n","| Faithfulness        | No                     |\n","| Answer Relevancy    | No                     |\n","| Context Precision   | Depends on variant     |\n","| Context Recall      | Generally yes          |\n","| Factual Correctness | Yes                    |\n","| Semantic Similarity | Yes                    |\n","\n","This distinction is particularly important when evaluating production data without human-labeled answers.\n","\n","## RAGAS metrics\n","\n","RAGAS provides a wide range of metrics. The most important metrics for conventional RAG evaluation are the following four. Additional metrics can evaluate answer correctness, noise sensitivity, entity recall, and other dimensions.\n","\n","**Generation**\n","\n","1. Faithfulness: Is the answer supported by retrieved context?\n","2. Answer relevancy: Does the answer address the user's question?\n","\n","**Retrieval**\n","\n","1. Context precision: Are the retrieved chunks relevant and well-ranked?\n","2. Context recall: Did retrieval find all information needed to answer?\n","\n","### Faithfulness\n","\n","It detect Hallucination. Faithfulness measures whether the generated answer is factually supported by the retrieved context. It does not primarily compare the answer against a ground-truth answer. Instead, it checks the answer against the information retrieved by the RAG system.\n","\n","**Formula**\n","\n","$$ \\text{Faithfulness} = \\frac{\\text{Number of supported claims}} {\\text{Total number of claims}} $$\n","\n","**Example**\n","\n","Question:\n","\n","> What is the refund period?\n","\n","Retrieved context:\n","\n","> ABC Company provides refunds within 30 days of purchase.\n","\n","Generated answer:\n","\n","> ABC Company provides refunds within 30 days. Refunds are available for 60 days. Customers can request refunds online.\n","\n","The generated answer contains three claims:\n","\n","| Claim                           | Supported by context? |\n","| ------------------------------- | --------------------- |\n","| Refunds within 30 days          | Yes                   |\n","| Refunds within 60 days          | No                    |\n","| Refunds can be requested online | No                    |\n","\n","Therefore:\n","\n","$$ \\text{Faithfulness} = \\frac{1}{3} = 0.33 $$\n","\n","Score: 0.33\n","\n","**How RAGAS evaluates faithfulness**\n","\n","The typical LLM-based evaluation process is:\n","\n","![Faithfullness Pipeline](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/masum184e/handbook/main/static/img/ai-engineering/ragas_faithfullness_pipeline.png)\n","\n","The LLM judge determines which claims can be inferred from the context. The score is the proportion of claims judged to be supported.&#x20;\n","\n","**Important points**\n","\n","- A high faithfulness score indicates that the answer is grounded in retrieved information.\n","- A low score may indicate hallucination or an incomplete/incorrect context.\n","- Faithfulness does not prove that the retrieved context itself is factually true.\n","- A correct answer based on the model's own knowledge may still receive a low score if that information is absent from the retrieved context."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":49,"id":"45fb9d67","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.548031Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.547658Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.800554Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.799181Z"},"papermill":{"duration":11.267586,"end_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.802884+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:19.535298+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Note: you may need to restart the kernel to use updated packages.\n"]}],"source":["pip install -q ragas "]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":50,"id":"d8a95e36","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.828239Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.82781Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.83395Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.832939Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.021908,"end_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.83618+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.814272+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["# from ragas import evaluate\n","\n","# from ragas.metrics import (\n","#     faithfulness,\n","#     answer_relevancy,\n","#     context_precision,\n","#     context_recall,\n","#     AnswerCorrectness\n","# )\n","\n","# result = evaluate(\n","#     dataset=dataset,\n","#     metrics=[\n","#         faithfulness,\n","#         answer_relevancy,\n","#         context_precision,\n","#         context_recall\n","#     ],\n","#     llm=llm,\n","#     embeddings=embeddings\n","# )"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":51,"id":"c339d4f1","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.862021Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.861629Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.86635Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.865282Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.020437,"end_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.868364+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.847927+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["# result"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":52,"id":"cbf1a604","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.893411Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.89302Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.898103Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.89687Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.020631,"end_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.900321+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.87969+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["# result[\"faithfulness\"]"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"e20f5e80","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.011118,"end_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.922651+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.911533+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Answer Relevancy\n","\n","It align Question-answer. Answer relevancy evaluates how directly the generated answer addresses the user's question. It checks whether the answer is relevant, complete, and focused on the requested information.\n","\n","**Example**\n","\n","Question:\n","\n","> What is the capital of Bangladesh?\n","\n","Answer A:\n","\n","> The capital of Bangladesh is Dhaka.\n","\n","Answer B:\n","\n","> Bangladesh is a country in South Asia. It has a large population, many rivers, and a rich cultural heritage.\n","\n","Answer A is highly relevant.\n","\n","Answer B contains useful information about Bangladesh but does not answer the actual question. Therefore, Answer A should receive a higher answer relevancy score.\n","\n","**Formula**\n","\n","A commonly used formulation is:\n","\n","$$ AR = \\frac{1}{N}\\sum_{i=1}^{N} \\cos(E_{q_i}, E_q) $$\n","\n","Where:\n","\n","- $AR$ = Answer Relevancy.\n","- $N$ = Number of generated candidate questions.\n","- $q_i$ = Question generated from the answer.\n","- $E_{q_i}$ = Embedding of generated question.\n","- $E_q$ = Embedding of original question.\n","- $cos$ = Cosine similarity.\n","\n","**How it works**\n","\n","![Answer Relevancy](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/masum184e/handbook/main/static/img/ai-engineering/ragas_answer_relevancy.png)\n","\n","For example:\n","\n","Original question:\n","\n","> What is machine learning?\n","\n","Generated answer:\n","\n","> Machine learning is a subset of AI that allows systems to learn patterns from data.\n","\n","The evaluator may generate candidate questions such as:\n","\n","- What is machine learning?\n","- How do machines learn from data?\n","- What is the relationship between machine learning and AI?\n","\n","These candidate questions are compared semantically against the original question.\n","\n","**Important distinction**\n","\n","Answer relevancy is not the same as factual correctness. A response can be relevant but factually wrong.\n","\n","Example:\n","\n","Question:\n","\n","> What is the capital of Bangladesh?\n","\n","Answer:\n","\n","> The capital of Bangladesh is Chittagong.\n","\n","This answer is directly relevant to the question, but incorrect. Thus, answer relevancy alone cannot detect this error."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":53,"id":"05ccb5e5","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.94766Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.947229Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.951929Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.950769Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.019405,"end_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.954003+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.934598+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["# result[\"answer_relevancy\"]"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"983a5339","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.011155,"end_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.97688+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.965725+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Context Precision\n","\n","Context precision measures whether the retrieved documents are relevant to the user's question, especially whether relevant documents are ranked near the top.\n","\n","It helps determine if the retriever is returning useful chunks or unnecessary information.\n","\n","**Example**\n","\n","Question:\n","\n","> What is the refund period?\n","\n","Suppose the retriever returns five chunks:\n","\n","| Rank | Retrieved chunk          | Relevant? |\n","| ---- | ------------------------ | --------- |\n","| 1    | Refund period is 30 days | Yes       |\n","| 2    | Company history          | No        |\n","| 3    | Refund eligibility rules | Yes       |\n","| 4    | Employee salary policy   | No        |\n","| 5    | Refund processing steps  | Yes       |\n","\n","The retrieval system has found three relevant chunks, but two irrelevant chunks are mixed in.\n","\n","Context precision rewards useful chunks that appear earlier.\n","\n","**Formula**\n","\n","The common reference-based Context Precision\\@K formulation is:\n","\n","$$\n","\\text{CP@K} =\n","\\frac{\\displaystyle\\sum_{k=1}^{K}\n","P@k \\cdot v_k}\n","{\\displaystyle\\sum_{k=1}^{K} v_k}\n","$$\n","\n","Where:\n","\n","- $P@k$ = Precision at rank $k$.\n","- $v_k$ = 1 if the chunk at rank $k$ is relevant; otherwise, 0.\n","- $K$ = Total number of retrieved chunks.\n","\n","**Simple calculation**\n","\n","Consider this retrieval sequence:\n","\n","1. Relevant chunk\n","2. Irrelevant chunk\n","3. Relevant chunk\n","4. Irrelevant chunk\n","\n","Precision at each relevant rank:\n","\n","- At rank 1: $P@1 = 1/1 = 1.0$\n","- At rank 3: $P@3 = 2/3 = 0.667$\n","\n","Thus:\n","\n","$$ CP@4 = \\frac{1 + 0.667}{2} $$\n","\n","$$ CP@4 \\approx 0.833 $$\n","\n","Score: 0.833\n","\n","**Why context precision is important**\n","\n","High context precision means:\n","\n","- The retriever is returning relevant information.\n","- Less irrelevant information is passed to the LLM.\n","- The LLM has a more focused context.\n","- Token consumption may decrease.\n","- The answer quality may improve.\n","\n","Context precision is useful when tuning:\n","\n","- Vector similarity thresholds.\n","- Top-k retrieval.\n","- Hybrid search.\n","- Reranking models.\n","- Chunk size.\n","- Metadata filters."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":54,"id":"bde268e9","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.001418Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.000973Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.005537Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.00457Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.019497,"end_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.007535+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:30.988038+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["# result[\"context_precision\"]"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"efa5cd83","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.01108,"end_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.029772+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.018692+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Context Recall\n","\n","Context recall measures whether the retrieved context contains all the necessary information required to produce the reference answer. It is generally evaluated using a ground-truth/reference answer.\n","\n","**Example**\n","\n","Question:\n","\n","> What are the three benefits of exercise?\n","\n","Ground-truth answer:\n","\n","> Exercise improves cardiovascular health, strengthens muscles, and improves mental health.\n","\n","Retrieved context:\n","\n","> Exercise improves cardiovascular health and strengthens muscles.\n","\n","The retriever found two of the three required pieces of information.\n","\n","**Formula**\n","\n","A simplified conceptual formula is:\n","\n","$$ \\text{Context Recall} = \\frac{\\text{Reference claims supported by context}} {\\text{Total reference claims}} $$\n","\n","Therefore:\n","\n","$$ CR = \\frac{2}{3} = 0.667 $$\n","\n","Score: 0.667\n","\n","**How RAGAS evaluates context recall**\n","\n","![Context Recall](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/masum184e/handbook/main/static/img/ai-engineering/ragas_context_recall.png)\n","\n","The evaluator checks whether each reference claim can be supported by the retrieved contexts.&#x20;\n","\n","**Context recall vs context precision**\n","\n","| Context precision                           | Context recall                                   |\n","| ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n","| Measures relevance of retrieved chunks      | Measures coverage of necessary information       |\n","| Focuses on retrieval quality and ranking    | Focuses on completeness                          |\n","| Low score means too much irrelevant context | Low score means important information is missing |\n","| Helps optimize reranking and search         | Helps optimize retrieval coverage and top-k      |"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":55,"id":"e7d6b86a","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.05388Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.05348Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.057815Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.056944Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.018837,"end_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.059742+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.040905+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["# result[\"context_recall\"]"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"439824da","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-17T16:47:29.478498Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-17T16:47:29.474938Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-17T16:47:29.495136Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-17T16:47:29.493148Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-17T16:47:29.478405Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.011085,"end_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.082631+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.071546+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Additional Metrics\n","\n","Beyond the four main metrics, RAGAS includes additional metrics for more comprehensive evaluation.\n","\n","\n","### Answer Correctness / Factual Correctness\n","\n","This metric evaluates whether the generated answer matches the reference answer in terms of factual content.\n","\n","Example:\n","\n","Ground truth:\n","\n","> The capital of Bangladesh is Dhaka.\n","\n","Generated answer:\n","\n","> Dhaka is the capital city of Bangladesh.\n","\n","The answers express the same fact, so correctness should be high.\n","\n","But if the generated answer is:\n","\n","> The capital of Bangladesh is Chittagong.\n","\n","The score should be low.\n","\n","RAGAS's Factual Correctness metric can compare factual claims using precision and recall:\n","\n","$$ F1 = \\frac{2 \\times Precision \\times Recall} {Precision + Recall} $$\n","\n","This metric generally requires a reference answer."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":56,"id":"9bdebc17","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.106669Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.10626Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.110778Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.109748Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.019038,"end_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.11281+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.093772+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["# result[\"context_recall\"]"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"9d0b0987","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.011974,"end_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.135915+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.123941+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Context Entity Recall\n","\n","Context Entity Recall evaluates how many important entities in the reference answer appear in the retrieved context.\n","\n","Entities may include:\n","\n","- People\n","- Organizations\n","- Locations\n","- Dates\n","- Products\n","- Technical terms\n","\n","Example:\n","\n","Reference answer:\n","\n","> OpenAI was founded in 2015 in the United States.\n","\n","Retrieved context:\n","\n","> OpenAI is an AI research and deployment organization.\n","\n","The context may omit the founding date and location. Entity recall can help identify this missing information."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"e276bf70","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.011598,"end_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.15891+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.147312+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Noise Sensitivity\n","\n","Noise Sensitivity measures how sensitive the generated answer is to irrelevant or misleading information in the retrieved context.\n","\n","For example:\n","\n","Question:\n","\n","> What is the company's refund period?\n","\n","Relevant context:\n","\n","> The refund period is 30 days.\n","\n","Irrelevant context:\n","\n","> The company was founded in 2005.\n","\n","If the generated answer starts talking about the company's history instead of the refund policy, the system is sensitive to retrieval noise.\n","\n","Noise Sensitivity is useful when:\n","\n","- The knowledge base contains many unrelated documents.\n","- Retrieval returns too many chunks.\n","- There are conflicting documents.\n","- You want to improve robustness against misleading context."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"6b55bd0f","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.010952,"end_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.181577+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.170625+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Semantic Similarity\n","\n","Semantic Similarity measures how close the generated answer is to a reference answer in meaning, typically using embeddings.\n","\n","Example:\n","\n","Reference:\n","\n","> A neural network learns patterns from data.\n","\n","Generated:\n","\n","> Neural networks identify and learn relationships within datasets.\n","\n","The wording differs, but the meaning is similar.\n","\n","Semantic similarity is useful when exact string matching is not appropriate."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"662e3b11","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.011682,"end_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.205901+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.194219+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Summarization metrics\n","\n","RAGAS also supports evaluating summarization tasks.\n","\n","It can evaluate aspects such as:\n","\n","- Summary quality.\n","- Factual consistency.\n","- Coverage.\n","- Conciseness."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"a5ff8327","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.011141,"end_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.228545+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-23T06:11:31.217404+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Agent evaluation metrics\n","\n","RAGAS is not limited to RAG chatbots. Its metric library also covers AI agents.\n","\n","Examples include:\n","\n","| Metric              | What it evaluates                                  |\n","| ------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n","| Tool Call Accuracy  | Whether the agent selected the correct tool        |\n","| Tool Call F1        | Precision and recall of tool calls                 |\n","| Agent Goal Accuracy | Whether the agent achieved the requested goal      |\n","| Topic Adherence     | Whether the agent stayed within the intended topic |\n","\n","These metrics are useful in applications involving agents that interact with APIs, databases, and external tools.\n","\n","## Interpret RAGAS scores\n","\n","A high RAGAS score is generally desirable, but the interpretation depends on the metric and evaluation dataset.\n","\n","A common starting point for interpreting scores:\n","\n","| Score      | General interpretation |\n","| ---------- | ---------------------- |\n","| 0.90–1.00  | Excellent              |\n","| 0.80–0.89  | Good                   |\n","| 0.60–0.79  | Needs improvement      |\n","| Below 0.60 | Poor                   |\n","\n","These are informal guidelines, not universal RAGAS acceptance thresholds. Establish thresholds based on your use case, data quality, and human-validated evaluation results.\n","\n","For example, a medical or financial RAG system may need much stricter evaluation than a general-purpose educational chatbot.\n","\n","## Diagnosing\n","\n","This is one of the most useful practical applications of RAGAS.\n","\n","![Context Recall](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/masum184e/handbook/main/static/img/ai-engineering/ragas_diagnosing.png)\n","\n","### Common problems and solutions\n","\n","| Problem                               | Possible solution                                                    |\n","| ------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n","| Low faithfulness                      | Improve prompt grounding, remove contradictory contexts              |\n","| Low answer relevancy                  | Improve query handling and answer instructions                       |\n","| Low context precision                 | Add reranking, adjust top-k, improve chunking                        |\n","| Low context recall                    | Increase top-k, improve embedding model, use hybrid search           |\n","| High precision but low recall         | Retrieve more relevant chunks                                        |\n","| High recall but low precision         | Reduce noise, improve ranking                                        |\n","| High faithfulness but low correctness | Check whether retrieved documents are themselves wrong or incomplete |\n","\n","One of the key lessons is that improving the LLM does not necessarily improve the RAG system. The retrieval component may be the actual bottleneck.\n","\n","## RAGAS vs traditional evaluation\n","\n","| Feature                   | Traditional evaluation  | RAGAS                        |\n","| ------------------------- | ----------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n","| Exact string matching     | Yes                     | Supported                    |\n","| BLEU / ROUGE              | Yes                     | Supported                    |\n","| Semantic evaluation       | Limited                 | Supported                    |\n","| Hallucination detection   | Difficult               | Faithfulness metric          |\n","| Retrieval evaluation      | Requires custom methods | Context precision and recall |\n","| LLM-as-a-judge            | Usually custom          | Built-in metrics             |\n","| Custom evaluation metrics | Possible                | Supported                    |\n","| RAG-specific evaluation   | Limited                 | Designed for it              |\n","\n","Traditional metrics often work well for structured outputs or exact-match tasks.\n","\n","RAGAS is particularly useful for natural language answers where multiple different wordings can express the same correct information.\n","\n","## Advantages\n","\n","* **Automated evaluation**: Reduces the need for manually checking every generated answer.\n","* **Component-wise analysis**: Evaluates both retrieval and generation.\n","* **Flexible metrics**: Supports different tasks, including RAG, agent evaluation, and general LLM applications.\n","* **Continuous improvement**: Can be integrated into testing and development workflows.\n","* **Customizable**: Developers can create custom evaluation metrics.\n","\n","## Limitations\n","\n","RAGAS is powerful, but it is not perfect.\n","\n","### LLM judge bias\n","\n","The evaluator is itself an LLM. It may make mistakes when judging factual correctness or relevance.\n","\n","### Evaluation cost**\n","\n","LLM-based metrics may require multiple model calls per question. Evaluating a large dataset can incur significant cost.\n","\n","### Non-deterministic scores\n","\n","Scores may change depending on:\n","\n","- Evaluator model.\n","- Prompt wording.\n","- Model temperature.\n","- Dataset.\n","- RAGAS version.\n","\n","### Ground truth quality\n","\n","If the reference answers are wrong, context recall and factual correctness can be misleading.\n","\n","### Scores are not absolute truth\n","\n","A faithfulness score of 0.95 does not mean that 95% of all production answers are guaranteed to be correct.\n","\n","RAGAS scores should be calibrated against human judgments and real-world outcomes."]}],"metadata":{"kaggle":{"accelerator":"none","dataSources":[],"isInternetEnabled":true,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebo